`verilator_config
// PeakRDL generates one always_comb per field, and each writes a different
// sub-field of the same `field_combo` struct. No two blocks touch the same
// bits, but Verilator's IEEE 1800-2023 9.2.2.2 check works at variable
// granularity and cannot prove that, so it reports MULTIDRIVEN -- 128 times
// in the bridge, all of them this one struct in one generated regblock.
// Vivado, Synopsys DC and Icarus accept the pattern silently.
//
// Waiving only the generated regblock keeps MULTIDRIVEN live everywhere else,
// which matters: a genuine two-driver net in the crossbar is exactly what this
// gate should catch. This file lives outside generated/ so regeneration does
// not overwrite it. Same treatment as misc/rtl/regs/obs_regs.vlt and
// stream/regs/stream_regs.vlt.
lint_off -rule MULTIDRIVEN -file "*_regblock_mon_cfg.sv"
